ETS) {\n      evaluateCell(x + dx, y + dy);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return [...next.values()];\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784966651683},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_433e16f1c4b540cd82d4e926","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-50-40_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-2\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-50-40_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-2\n\n ✓ src/game-of-life.spec.ts  (9 tests) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n   Start at  08:04:11\n   Duration  150ms (transform 26ms, setup 0ms, collect 23ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784966651683},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 9 tests still pass. Let me verify correctness of the boolean simplification once more (I did this in my head earlier):\n\nOriginal: `(alive && (count === 2 || count === 3)) || (!alive && count === 3)`\nNew: `count === 3 || (alive && count === 2)`\n\n- count===3 → both true regardless of alive. ✓ (covers alive+3 survive, and dead+3 birth)\n- alive && count===2 → original: alive && (2||3) with count=2 = alive && true = alive; new: alive && true = alive. ✓\n- alive && count=4: original alive&&(F||F)=F; new F||(alive&&F)=F ✓\n- alive && count=1: F ✓\n- dead && count=2: original (!alive && 3)=F, and alive&&...=F → F; new 3?F, alive&&2 → F&&T=F → F ✓\n\nAll consistent, and tests confirm. \n\nNow let me write the final report with the new mass calculation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 9 tests remain green. The boolean simplification is provably equivalent (and verified by the test suite covering all rule branches: underpopulation, survival-2, survival-3, reproduction, overpopulation).\n\n## Step 5: New APP Mass (decision region)\n\n**Refactored