ate the impl — that's the red 1 stage 1.\n\n  Let me write it.\n\n  For the test descriptions, I'll include expected values per the skill.\n\n  Let me write the spec file:\n\n  ```ts\n  import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n  import { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n  import type { Cell } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\n  describe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"returns empty array for empty input -- [] -> []\");\n    it.todo(\"a single isolated live cell dies (underpopulation, 0 neighbors) -- [(0,0)] -> []\");\n    it.todo(\"two adjacent live cells each die (underpopulation, 1 neighbor) -- [(0,1),(1,1)] -> []\");\n    it.todo(\"a 2x2 block still life is unchanged (survival, 3 neighbors, no births) -- [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] -> same\");\n    it.todo(\"a dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbors is born (reproduction) -- [(0,2),(1,2),(0,1)] -> [(0,2),(1,2),(0,1),(1,1)]\");\n    it.todo(\"a vertical blinker becomes horizontal (survival 2 + reproduction + underpopulation) -- [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] -> [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\");\n    it.todo(\"a live cell with 4 live neighbors dies and is absent from output (overpopulation) -- center (1,1) absent, survivor (0,2) present\");\n    it.todo(\"handles negative coordinates -- blinker at [(-2,-2),(-2,-1),(-2,0)] -> [(-3,-1),(-2,-1),(-1,-1)]\");\n    it.todo(\"blinker returns to its original shape after two generations (oscillator period 2) -- nextGeneration(nextGeneration(vertical)) == vertical\");\n  });\n  ```\n\n  Wait, importing `type { Cell }` — I need to export `Cell` type from the impl. The API contract says `type Cell = [number, number]; export function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[];`. So I should export Cell. I'll export `export type Cell = [number, number];`. Good. But for the stub/first red, the file doesn't exist → import error. Fine.\n\n  Actually, do I need to import Cell type in the spec? I can use `[number, number]` inline or define a local type. To avoid co