n (its conditional, `Set` construction, and `every` loop). The index is now built once at module load instead of reconstructed per call.\n- **Rule 1**: All 7 tests green; `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n**Design boundary respected**: This refactoring intentionally stays within the example-mapping paradigm (a keyed lookup table of known pattern→successor pairs). It does *not* implement the general neighbor-counting algorithm — the two remaining `it.todo` tests (translated blinker at negative coordinates; period-2 oscillation) are designed to force that generalization in future Red/Green cycles, and preempting it would subvert the experiment.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Replaced per-call linear scan + `Set`-based `sameCells` with a module-load `Map` index keyed by a canonical (sorted) cell-set key; `nextGeneration` reduced to a single lookup.\n**Mass Change**: 61 → 38 (Δ −23); per-call 24 → 7\n**Tests**: All 7 passing (2 todo), `tsc --noEmit` clean"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-50-40_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: nextGeneration now also recognizes the overpopulation example [(0,2),(1,2),(2,2),(1,1),(0,0),(1,0),(2,0)] and returns its 8-cell next generation (center (1,1) dies; (1,3) and (1,-1) are born). Four hardcoded named patterns now exist in a PATTERN_TRANSITIONS lookup table.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: nextGeneration now also recognizes the overpopulation example [(0,2),(1,2),(